Seed corpora, one directory per fuzz target.

These are committed; `fuzz/corpus/', which is what the fuzzer grows from
them, is not -- it reached 34MB and five thousand files in three minutes of
running, and none of it is worth reviewing.

Each seed is a real input, truncated to three kilobytes: a page from the
fixture sites for `frontmatter' and `markdown', a page that uses a directive
for `directives', and a rendered page for `links'.  A seed is a starting
point for mutation rather than a document, so the truncation costs nothing
and the size of the repository is a real thing.

To add one, put the input in the right directory under any name.  When a
fuzz run finds a crash, cargo-fuzz writes the input to `fuzz/artifacts/';
turn it into a named unit test first, then add it here so the fuzzer starts
from it in future.

